The '''Chaos Temple''' is a temple of [[Zamorak]] located around level 11 Wilderness, north of [[Varrock]]. The entire building is near-completely surrounded by molten lava which frequently ejects flaming rocks that do minor damage to anyone nearby where they land. The area is also [[multi-combat]], and contains many [[Elder Chaos druid|elder chaos druids]] who will [[teleblock]] any players who get too close.

The pattern on the floor hints that the temple may once have been dedicated to [[Zaros]], which is plausible given that many of his fortresses and outposts in the Second Age were in what is now the Wilderness, and were destroyed and/or aligned to different [[gods]] during and after the [[God Wars]].

Players will receive the following message the first time they enter the Chaos Temple each day:
{{Mes|WARNING: |color=red}}{{Mes|Elder Chaos druids can ignore the immunity period and cast |color=black}}{{Mes|Tele Block |color=purple}}{{Mes|on you before it expires.|color=black}}

==Transportation==
* [[Burning amulet]] teleport to the north entrance in level 15 Wilderness.
* [[Ring of dueling]] teleport to [[Ferox Enclave]], and run east.
* Run north from [[Varrock]] or north-east from the [[Grand Exchange]], crossing the [[wilderness ditch]].

==Features==
===Free-to-play===
In [[free-to-play]], there are no monsters present in the temple, so the only features available to free players are the [[bones|bone]] spawns which can be picked up and buried to train [[Prayer]], and a [[chaos altar (Prayer)|chaos altar]] which can be prayed at to restore Prayer.

===Members===
The temple itself becomes significantly more dangerous in members' worlds, as it is populated by numerous [[Elder Chaos druid|elder chaos druids]] that can deal hefty damage, cast [[teleblock]] to players, and frequently teleport players to them, making escape difficult if multiple druids are attacking a player. Many [[zombie pirate]]s also spawn around the temple, frequently engaging in combat with the druids.

The zombie pirates can be killed for lucrative drops, including [[teleport anchoring scroll]]s which can be used to stop the elder chaos druids from teleporting you, and [[zombie pirate key]]s, which can be used to open the [[Zombie Pirate's Locker]]s located in [[Pyre Cove]] to the east of the temple.

[[Simon]], a [[cape merchants|cape merchant]], can usually be found in or near the temple selling [[team cape]]s 9, 19, 29, 39, and 49 with the teardrop pattern.

A [[Hunter|hunting]] location with [[black salamander]]s can be found north-east of the temple.

